{"schema": "m2-event/0", "run_id": "run_78e703387021", "seq": 16, "ts": "2026-09-22T09:30:56.479703+00:00", "kind": "proposed_effect", "proposed_effect_id": "pe_823ffc1ff246", "invocation_id": "inv_56177d225e74", "effect_type": 1, "effect_type_name": "workspace_mutation", "payload_ref": "write:ledger.py>>>\"\"\"\nBalance transfers.\n\"\"\"\nAUDIT = []\n\n\ndef _audit_line(src, dst, amt):\n    # builds the line one character at a time; this is the slow part\n    out = \"\"\n    for ch in f\"transfer {src}->{dst} {amt}\":\n        out = out + ch\n    return out\n\n\ndef transfer(book, src, dst, amt):\n    \"\"\"Move amt from src to dst, leaving an audit entry.\"\"\"\n    if book.get(src, 0) < amt:\n        raise ValueError(\"insufficient funds\")\n    book[src] -= amt\n    book[dst] = book.get(dst, 0) + amt\n    AUDIT.append(_audit_line(src, dst, amt))\n    return book\n\n\n# OBJECTIVE\nreplace AUDIT.append with a more efficient append method\nCurrent state still fails:\nthe audit line is still built one character at a time\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n- follow it exactly.\n- For every file you create or change, emit one block (give the WHOLE file, never a diff):\n<<<FILE path=ledger.py>>>...the full new file content...<<<ENDFILE>>\nThen, as the very last thing in your reply, emit exactly one control block:\n<<<CONTROL>>>...<<<ENDCONTROL", "disposition": "realized", "links": {}}
